# Location Selection Checklist for UK Convenience Stores

**A practical checklist to validate high-potential convenience store sites**

---

## Catchment and Demographics

- [ ] Population within 5–10 minute walk
- [ ] Daytime population density
- [ ] Household income levels
- [ ] Age demographics and family composition
- [ ] Residential vs commercial mix

## Competition and Complementary Retail

- [ ] Number of direct competitors within catchment area
- [ ] Complementary services nearby (transport, offices, schools)
- [ ] Gaps in current convenience retail offer
- [ ] Market saturation analysis
- [ ] Competitor pricing and product range

## Accessibility and Transport

- [ ] Main pedestrian routes and footfall patterns
- [ ] Parking availability and restrictions
- [ ] Cycle access and facilities
- [ ] Public transport links (bus stops, train stations)
- [ ] Visibility from main roads
- [ ] Ease of access for deliveries

## Physical Assessment

- [ ] Frontage visibility and signage opportunities
- [ ] Unit depth and floor area (minimum 800-1000 sq ft recommended)
- [ ] Ceiling height and natural light
- [ ] Servicing access and delivery arrangements
- [ ] Condition of property and required refurbishment works
- [ ] Layout suitability for retail use

## Planning and Compliance

- [ ] Class use permissions (A1/E class for retail)
- [ ] Local Plan constraints and restrictions
- [ ] Listed building or conservation area status
- [ ] Licensing requirements (alcohol, tobacco, lottery)
- [ ] Building regulations compliance
- [ ] Health and safety requirements
- [ ] Disability access compliance

## Commercial Terms

- [ ] Rent and service charge levels
- [ ] Break clauses and rent review periods
- [ ] Landlord fit-out contribution availability
- [ ] Lease length and security of tenure
- [ ] Rates liability and assessment
- [ ] Insurance requirements

## Financial Filters

- [ ] Estimated weekly sales projection
- [ ] Break-even analysis completed
- [ ] Payback period calculation (target: 18-24 months)
- [ ] Capital expenditure estimate
- [ ] Working capital requirements
- [ ] Funding sources identified

---

## Quick Decision Scorecard

Rate each category above from 1-5 (5 being excellent):

- **Catchment & Demographics:** ___/5
- **Competition:** ___/5
- **Accessibility:** ___/5
- **Physical Property:** ___/5
- **Planning & Compliance:** ___/5
- **Commercial Terms:** ___/5
- **Financial Viability:** ___/5

**Total Score:** ___/35

### Decision Guidelines:
- **30-35 points:** Excellent location - proceed with confidence
- **25-29 points:** Good location - address any weak areas
- **20-24 points:** Marginal - requires significant improvements
- **Below 20:** High risk - consider alternative locations

